          <!-- 2026-10-06e：标题两行改用美工字图（21/22.png 紧裁，中文原标题译为英文由美工出图）；
               2026-10-06f：正文段落/列表由中文译为英文（保持未来时态，不写成已完成结果）；
               本屏内容加宽至约 60% 页宽、间距拉开（static/css/index.css 搜 fv- 与 #future-vision） -->
          <h2 class="sr-only">Future Vision: From H1N1 to the Broad Spectrum Platform</h2>
          <img class="fv-title-img reveal" src="static/image/Animation/index/webp/ninth-section/future-vision-title.png"
            alt="Future Vision" width="1056" height="529" decoding="async">
          <img class="fv-sub-img reveal" src="static/image/Animation/index/webp/ninth-section/future-vision-subtitle.png"
            alt="From H1N1 to the Broad Spectrum Platform" width="1219" height="88" decoding="async">
          <p class="reveal">
            Once the H1N1 proof of concept is complete, the core value of the PAGER-Yeast platform lies in its
            modularity and replaceability: the membrane nanobody recognition unit can be rapidly iterated against
            new antigens, while the downstream GPCR signal-rewiring and the dual-mode reporter system stay
            universal. Combined with a low-cost portable fluorescence reader, the system could move from a
            laboratory prototype to a field-ready testing tool for primary-care settings.
          </p>
          <ul class="yeast-screen__list reveal">
            <li><strong>Modular recognition unit:</strong> keeping the α-factor secretion anchor and linker
              scaffold, swapping only the VHH sequence would extend coverage to H5, H7 and other influenza
              subtypes — and potentially to respiratory pathogens such as SARS-CoV-2 and RSV;</li>
            <li><strong>Signal optimization:</strong> by tuning the DCZ concentration gradient and induction
              time, we plan to correlate fluorescence intensity with viral load for semi-quantitative detection
              that matches portable fluorimeters;</li>
            <li><strong>Multi-scenario use:</strong> aimed at settings that need fast, low-cost results —
              primary-care clinic screening, school morning checks, border quarantine ports and at-home
              self-testing;</li>
            <li><strong>Open source &amp; standardization:</strong> submitting standardized biological parts
              (promoters, reporter genes, signaling modules) in an iGEM Registry-compatible form, together with
              reproducible protocols and plasmid maps.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="yeast-screen__placeholder reveal">[To be added: target subtype list, hardware prototype
            specifications, product timeline and a preliminary regulatory pathway assessment]</p>
        </div>
